omize tooltip with tokens, mind that these tokens are case sensitive.\"}]\n1c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"[class] – will be replaced with class text\"}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"[status] – will be replaced with status text\"}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"[note] -will be replaced with note\"}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"say you have a pattern like [class] | [note] | [status]\"}]\n20:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"then you will see something like Death Knight | Blood | Medium when you roll your mouse cursor onto a recruitment item\"}]\n21:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"(it will get everything inside that particular text box, if you put some html tags in that text box, it will show up as well, it maybe improved if this feature is becoming popular)\"}]\n22:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"— you can customize tooltip with tokens, mind that these tokens are case sensitive.[class] – will be replaced with class text[status] – will be replaced with status text[note] -will be replaced with notesay you have a pattern like [class] | [note] | [status]then you will see something like Death Knight | Blood | Medium when you roll your mouse cursor onto a recruitment item\"}]\n23:[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"id\":\"class-default-texts-are-10-classes-in-wow\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#class-default-texts-are-10-classes-in-wow\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"tabIndex\":\"-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"icon icon-link\"}]}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Class: (default texts are 10 classes in WOW)\"}]]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"— so it is possible to make multiple entries for same class.\"}]\n25:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Status: consist of 4 status (default text: High, Medium, Low, Closed).\"}]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"— The class will not be displayed if status is Closed (unless it is set to display in admin settings).\"}]\n27:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Note: additional note for the recruitment message (usually for different spec of the class).\"}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"Plugin Settings (Settings > WOW Recruit Widget):\"}]}]}]\n29:[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"id\":\"use-custom-style-sheet\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#use-custom-style-sheet\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"tabIndex\":\"-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"icon icon-link\"}]}],[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Use Custom Style Sheet:\"}]]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"— checking this will stop default style sheet from loading\"}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Status texts: consist of 4 status�\"}]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"— default text: High, Medium, Low, Closed.\"}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"— “closed” status will show if “display?” is checked\"}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Class texts: consist of 10 class slots�\"}]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"–�default texts are 10 classes in WOW in English\"}]\n30:[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"id\":\"if-you-managed-to-find-bugs-or-typos-please-feel-free-to-leave-a-comment-here\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#if-you-managed-to-find-bugs-or-typos-please-feel-free-to-leave-a-comment-here\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"tabIndex\":\"-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"icon icon-link\"}]}],\"If you managed to find bugs or typos, please feel free to leave a comment here.\"]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"installation\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#installation\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"tabIndex\":\"-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"icon icon-link\"}]}],\"Installation\"]}]\n32:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"1. Unpack and Upload all files to the \\\\`/wp-content/plugins/wow-recruit-widget\\\\` directory 2. Activate the plugin through the ‘Plugins’ menu in WordPress 3. Drag ‘WOW Recruitment Widget’ to your sidebar 4. Enter details and done! 5. (optional) go to Settings > WOW Recruit Widget to set up all classes and status texts to your own language\"}]\n33:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"frequently-asked-questions\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#frequently-asked-questions\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"tabIndex\":\"-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"icon icon-link\"}]}],\"Frequently Asked Questions\"]}]\n34:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"= These color/font/size does not match my template, can I change them? =\"}]}]\n35:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Yes, copy all contents in the widget style.css to your theme style.css, then choose “Use Custom Style Sheet” in admin panel, and remember to point .wr-icon sprite to a correct image, i.e. if you want to use the default image sprite, change .wr-icon > background-image to\"}]\n36:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"url(../../plugins/wow-recruit-widget/img/class-sprite.png)\"}]\n37:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"or using absolute link\"}]\n38:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"url(http://{your site's url}/wp-content/plugins/wow-recruit-widget/img/class-sprite.png)\"}]\n39:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"= I don’t want the icon class note to layout like that, can I change it? =\"}]}]\n3a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Yes, all layouts are done with css, please refer to the latest plugin URL for some useful links and examples\"}]\n3b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"= Can I sort recruitment messages in another way? =\"}]}]\n3c:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Unfortunately no, please leave me a comment if you want this feature :).\"}]\n3d:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"bed-time-readings\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#bed-time-readings\",\"aria-hidden\":\"true\",\"tabIndex\":\"-1\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"icon icon-link\"}]}],\"Bed Time Readings…\"]}]\n3e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"It first started with a really simple widget only for displaying some recruitment message, since there was nearly no plugins doing something I want in the wordpress plugin directory, which look nice on my guild site, and can be used easily by not-so-IT officers in my own guild.\"}]\n3f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Since 1.1 -�seems there are quite a number of sites using this widget by that time, I thought it would be a bit boring if it is not customizable, after all I thought it would lost the point of having wonderful looking WordPress site if they all look like those Joomla WOW sites with the same set, same looking plugins out there, so it was then designed to be highly customizable with very little CSS techniques to meet most design needs for individual WordPress website/blog.\"}]\n40:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Since 1.2 -�seems some sites using this widget are based on non-english contents, it would look weird to have English only on this widget, so it was then designed to be customizable for almost all texts so you can enter any information into those “recruitment” slots, and thus able to achieve multilingual support or even easily tailored for non-world of warcraft related uses.\"}]\n41:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Since 1.3 – graphical layout seems to be a reasonable feature and it is used in a couple of similar plugin, but it does not make sense if there are no grouping (by class) and tooltip on rollover, so in this version I’ve added tooltip first, grouping requires quite a lot of rework, so I’ve put it to todo list for 1.4.\"}]\n42:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"pt-6 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"target\":\"_blank\",\"rel\":\"nofollow\",\"href\":\"https://mobile.twitter.com/search?q